  "rationale": "Prematurity, early onset respiratory distress, and grunting strongly indicate neonatal RDS, whose radiographic hallmark is small lung volumes with diffuse granularity and air bronchograms.",
  "optionExplanations": {
    "A": "Classic appearance of neonatal respiratory distress syndrome in a preterm infant.",
    "B": "More consistent with complete alveolar filling such as severe pneumonia or pulmonary oedema, not the classic preterm RDS pattern.",
    "C": "This infant is symptomatic, so the X-ray would not be normal.",
    "D": "A pneumothorax would show pleural air and hyperlucency, not diffuse granular opacification.",
    "E": "Perihilar infiltrates suggest conditions such as transient tachypnoea of the newborn rather than surfactant deficiency."
  },
